## Description

In this project, we are going to build a simple URL shortener. You may have heard of [bit.ly](https://bitly.com/) before. It is a good example of a URL shortener. URL shorteners reduce the length of long URLs. Users are redirected to the original URL when they use the short version of a URL. Usually, you need a backend service to create a URL shortener, but we will mimic the functionality with JavaScript.

Let's start by setting up the page with HTML tags.

First, put the first-level `heading` that says `URL Shortener`, so we know where we are. Second, add the `input` with the ID of `input-url` with the placeholder `Enter a url`. Next, add a `button` with the ID of `button-create` with the text `Create`. Lastly, you need to list the URLs ÔÇö create an ordered list with the ID of `list-url`.

Once the page is set up, the functionality is as follows:

- After entering a URL and clicking on the `Create` button, generate a random short URL;
- The short URL should start with `localhost/` and the random character set should be 5 characters long after `localhost`;
- Before creating the short URL, check whether the given URL is a valid one, such as: [https://example.com/123](https://example.com/1234). If not, show a paragraph saying `Please enter a valid url` in the body. You can use a regular expression pattern to check the validity;
- The short URL is a link that redirects to the **original link** in a new browser tab. So, use the original link as the `href` of the new short link;
- Show the original URL next to the short link as a text;
- Append the short link as a list item to the ordered list: `list-url`.

You can use the IDs we've provided to select the elements.

## Objectives

Your page should:

- Contain the first-level `heading` with the text `URL Shortener`;
- Contain `input` with the ID of `input-url` and the placeholder `Enter a url`;
- Contain a `button` with the ID of `button-create` and the text `Create`;
- Contain an `ordered list` with the ID of `list-url`;
- Display the new short link from inside the `list-url`;
- Contain a paragraph with text `Please enter a valid url` if the entered URL is invalid.

